WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.655
Governance establishes the policies, ownership, and oversight needed to manage agents across an organization.

2
00:00:06.655 --> 00:00:24.295
A useful program maintains an inventory of agents, accountable business and technical owners, intended use, risk tier, connected tools, data classes, model and prompt versions, approval requirements, monitoring expectations, and review dates.

3
00:00:24.295 --> 00:00:28.157
Unknown or ownerless agents are difficult to secure responsibly.

4
00:00:28.157 --> 00:00:41.507
Policies should address acceptable use, access management, data handling, retention, human oversight, audit requirements, incident escalation, third-party dependencies, and lifecycle management.

5
00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:46.416
Governance should also define which uses are prohibited or require additional review.

6
00:00:46.416 --> 00:00:57.052
These decisions connect technical controls to legal, compliance, privacy, safety, and business obligations without expecting the model to interpret policy on its own.

7
00:00:57.052 --> 00:01:00.794
Lifecycle controls matter because agent capabilities change.

8
00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:08.207
New tools, broader permissions, different models, additional data sources, or expanded user groups can alter risk.

9
00:01:08.207 --> 00:01:15.261
Significant changes should trigger updated threat modeling, testing, approvals, documentation, and monitoring.

10
00:01:15.261 --> 00:01:23.643
Retirement should include revoking credentials, disabling integrations, handling retained data, and preserving required records.

11
00:01:23.643 --> 00:01:28.941
Effective governance supports business value rather than treating every change as identical.

12
00:01:28.941 --> 00:01:32.004
Risk tiers can scale requirements to impact.

13
00:01:32.004 --> 00:01:39.238
Evidence from tests, logs, incidents, near misses, access reviews, and user feedback should inform decisions.

14
00:01:39.238 --> 00:01:46.462
Clear accountability ensures that someone can approve risk, respond to problems, and improve the system throughout its life.
